From 5c2f486dfd7caa62a41be6ed4887fcdaa6efbadf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 10:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(spec-decode): cohort-atomic verification budget,
 16..40-row cost band, and idle-wakeup burst coalescing

Upstream base: 1107 vLLM patch head 320021e3c4dbb202d911ab70e2cd924c75420488 (tree ed1bdb7a7684da33d403a055521ac0c4dd7ca670).

Rationale:
On switched TP6/TP7/TP8 runs at 16 concurrent streams, prose decode regressed ~10% in 1107 relative to the synchronized 1030 run (706.4 -> 637.9 tok/s on TP6, 685.6 -> 601.0 tok/s on TP7, 753.6 -> 658.9 tok/s on TP8) while code at 16 streams improved (+19.2% on TP6):
1. When an idle EngineCoreProc woke on the first request of a 16-stream burst, _process_input_queue() immediately dispatched Step 1 with Request 0 alone while the ZMQ input thread was still deserializing Requests 1..15 (1+15 prefill split).
2. Under --async-scheduling, CPU get_num_tokens() computed draft_budget from _stale_confidences (Step T-2) while GPU reallocate_drafts() invoked assign_draft_budget_kernel on _confidence_probs (Step T-1). Whenever Request 0 changed confidence between T-2 and T-1, the remaining budget for the 15 identical trailing requests was not divisible by 15, and 1-ULP BF16 tile-alignment differences plus index tie-breaking shattered the 15 trailing prose streams into 4 desynchronized sub-cohorts (2+8+2+4), tripling unique active MoE experts per layer across all 61 MoE layers and adding a ~300 ms straggler tail.
3. In 0746, _step_cost(rows) applied HIGH_ROW_COST_SCALE=0.55 to all rows > 16 without an upper ceiling, discounting every draft row at c16 (rows 17..96) and over-verifying low-yield 2nd/3rd prose drafts across the second 32-row CTA / MXFP8 block boundary (ver/d 1.496 -> 2.038, M=40 -> 56 CUDA graph).

Fix all three mechanisms:
1. Add _coalesce_idle_burst() in EngineCoreProc._process_input_queue() to briefly poll input_queue (0.3 ms initial, 0.5 ms per subsequent burst arrival up to max_num_seqs) when waking from idle so concurrent burst waves enter Step 1 together.
2. In AdaptiveVerificationManager.get_num_tokens(), group sampling requests at the same (num_computed_tokens, prefill_len, eligible_drafts) whose stale confidences agree within COHORT_CONFIDENCE_TOL=0.025 into synchronized cohorts, average their confidences, admit draft steps atomically per cohort, pass the cohort-uniform capacities directly to reallocate_drafts(), skip per-row device dead_rows when cohort-locked, and monotonically phase-lock any split leading group A (k_A=0, k_B=min(k_B, gap)) so trailing cohort B catches up without overshooting.
3. Bound the 0.55x coalesced row-cost discount to rows 17..40 (HIGH_ROW_COST_CEILING=40) with HIGH_ROW_COST_ABOVE_SCALE=0.78 above 40 rows, pruning low-yield 2nd/3rd prose drafts at c16 while preserving c1..c8 and high-confidence code-c16 verification.

Quality implications:
Target-model verification semantics are unchanged; only speculative draft verification budgets and idle-wakeup request coalescing change.

Tests:
- pytest tests/v1/spec_decode/test_adaptive_verification.py tests/v1/worker/test_dead_rows.py tests/v1/engine/test_late_admission.py tests/v1/engine/test_late_admission_sink.py tests/v1/worker/test_late_admission.py (77 passed, 1 skipped).

Upstream status:
Local speculative-decoding and engine-core scheduling optimization for GB10 clusters.
